nd the coarse atlas coast, not observed core positions or the source coastal endpoint near25.5S. Excludes northern branch, undercurrent, rings, SICC and uncertain Mozambique Channel/Agulhas continuations.\",\n    \"layer\": \"Upper-current contextual geography; no fixed-depth or velocity-derived axis reconstructed. Excludes the equatorward undercurrent.\",\n    \"time_convention\": \"Undated contextual geography described by Nauw et al.2008, citing earlier studies; not an April2001 axis, seasonal state, annual mean or operational position.\",\n    \"source_url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2007JC004639\",\n    \"source_locator\": \"Introduction paragraph2: southward flow along eastern Madagascar between approximately20S and Cape Sainte Marie near25deg30minS; paragraph6: unresolved downstream alternatives. Original publisher HTML inspected; no source figure or station coordinates digitized.\",\n    \"source_citation\": \"Nauw, van Aken, Webb, Lutjeharms and de Ruijter (2008), Observations of the southern East Madagascar Current and undercurrent and countercurrent system, Journal of Geophysical Research113,C08006, doi:10.1029/2007JC004639.\",\n    \"source_license\": \"Original OSW factual paraphrase and editorial vertices; no publication, figure, station data or provider geometry redistributed.\",\n    \"source_retrieved_date\": \"2026-10-21\",\n    \"protocol_file\": \"plans/southern-east-madagascar-reference-route-protocol-v2.md\",\n    \"coordinate_selection\": \"V1 rejected all27 scenarios on coarse land intersections; complete rejected input and attempts retained. V2 uses a declared farther-offshore corridor, including a26.1S Cape approach distinct from the source coastal point near25.5S. No bathymetric or current-axis verification. All27 cartographic sensitivities retained, no physical uncertainty or seasonal interpretation. No fitting to the published650km extent.\",\n    \"coordinates_lon_lat\": [\n      [\n        49.7,\n     